+### Tier B — local runs with the stub transport and a stand-in `claude` (no API call)
+
+#### Step 6 — Create the sandbox repository, the task file and the stand-in `claude` `[LOCAL-WRITE]`
+
+**Do:**
+
+```bash
+[ ! -e /tmp/d12 ] || echo "STOP: remove /tmp/d12 first"
+mkdir -p /tmp/d12/repo /tmp/d12/stub /tmp/d12/out && cd /tmp/d12/repo
+git init -q -b master . && printf 'hello\n' > app.txt && git add app.txt
+git -c user.name=d12 -c user.email=d12@example.invalid commit -q -m "d12 base"
+cat > TASK.md <<'EOF'
+---
+id: TASK-D12
+status: Doing
+---
+
+# Task: say hello
+
+- [x] Write app.txt
+- [ ] Final gate: superclaude reflect run TASK.md
+EOF
+cat > /tmp/d12/stub/claude <<'EOF'
+#!/bin/sh
+# Stand-in for the claude CLI. Reads the prompt from stdin and logs it. When
+# D12_SCORE is set, writes an adversarial return contract into the folder named
+# by the prompt's --output, then exits with D12_STUB_EXIT (default 0).
+prompt=$(cat)
+printf '%s\n' "$prompt" >> /tmp/d12/stub/prompts.log
+out=$(printf '%s\n' "$prompt" | sed -n 's/.* --output \([^ ]*\)$/\1/p')
+if [ -n "${D12_SCORE:-}" ] && [ -n "$out" ]; then
+  mkdir -p "$out/adversarial"
+  printf 'return_contract:\n  status: %s\n  convergence_score: %s\n' \
+    "${D12_ADV_STATUS:-success}" "$D12_SCORE" > "$out/adversarial/return-contract.yaml"
+fi
+exit "${D12_STUB_EXIT:-0}"
+EOF
+chmod +x /tmp/d12/stub/claude
+PATH="/tmp/d12/stub:$PATH" command -v claude
+git rev-parse HEAD
+```
+
+**Expected result:** no `STOP` line, then `/tmp/d12/stub/claude`, then the 40-character commit id. Write it down: later expected results call it `<HEAD>` and its first 12 characters `<HEAD12>`. The repository is on `master`, so the audit base (`git merge-base HEAD master`) is `<HEAD>`. The unchecked item is the gate line itself, which the phase check ignores. (source: base chain `config.py:81-109`; phase check `runner.py:313-370`; the scorer prompt ends with `--output <dir>`, `ensemble.py:582-598`)
